  "id": "46635d55-3b57-529d-b7f3-e22fb5d46a2d",
  "slug": "carrot-cake-cheesecake",
  "name": "Carrot Cake Cheesecake",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "This carrot cake cheesecake features a moist cake layer topped with a creamy filling. Each bite delivers two favorite dessert tastes in one forkful!",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Position the oven racks in the center and lower third of the oven. Fill a roasting pan halfway with water and place onto the lower rack. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Grease a 9-inch springform pan with cooking spray."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Make the cheesecake: Beat cream cheese in a large bowl with an electric mixer on high speed until fluffy. Add sugar and beat on medium-low speed for 2 minutes. Beat in eggs, one at a time, mixing well after each addition. Mix in sour cream and vanilla until smooth. Stir in flour and set aside."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Make the carrot cake: Beat brown sugar and oil in a second large bowl with an electric mixer on medium speed until smooth. Add egg and beat for 2 minutes. Mix in flour, cinnamon, baking powder, and salt on low speed until combined. Fold in carrots and walnuts."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Spread carrot cake batter into the prepared pan, then pour cheesecake batter over top."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Place cake into the preheated oven on the center rack (above the roasting pan with water). Bake until cheesecake is set, about 1 hour and 10 minutes, covering the top with aluminum foil if browning too quickly. Remove from the oven, place onto a wire rack, and let cool for 10 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Run a knife around the edge of the pan to loosen cake, then let cool to room temperature, about 50 minutes. Refrigerate until completely chilled, 8 hours to overnight."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Make the frosting: Beat confectioners' sugar, cream cheese, and almond extract in a medium bowl with an electric mixer until smooth."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Remove the ring of the pan. Spread frosting on top of chilled cheesecake layer."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 16,
